course: dictionary
lesson: 4465
title: Hardy: strong enough to survive
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Some horses need rugs in winter, especially clipped or thin-coated ones, while hardy ponies grow thick coats and may need no rug at all.» The sentence contrasts two kinds of horse. Horses that need rugs are not strong enough to manage the cold alone, so hardy must mean strong enough to cope without help.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «hardy ponies grow thick coats» becomes «ponies that can cope with cold grow thick coats». It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: The same word can describe plants and people. «A hardy plant» stays outside and survives winter frost. «A few hardy swimmers went into the icy sea» tells you they were brave and tough.
fact: Hardy means strong and able to live through hard conditions, such as cold, wind or little food.
fact: «Hardy» plants can stay outside in winter because they survive frost.
fact: «Hardy» can also mean brave and tough, as in «a few hardy swimmers went into the icy sea».
fact: The noun is hardiness, which means how well something can cope with tough conditions.
fact: Hardy is also a surname, as in the writer Thomas Hardy.
exercise: «Hardy ponies grow thick coats and may need no rug at all.» What does hardy mean here? | Always sleepy | Frightened of the snow | *Able to cope with cold without help | Very small and cute
exercise: In a garden, a «hardy plant» is one that | Grows only indoors | Has no leaves at all | *Stays outside and survives winter frost | Needs watering every hour
exercise: Which word could replace hardy in «a few hardy swimmers went into the icy sea»? | Sleepy | Shy | *Brave | Wet
test: Which noun comes from hardy? | *Hardiness | Hardware | Hardly | Harden
test: «Thomas Hardy» is a writer. In this name, what is Hardy? | *A surname | A kind of plant | A type of horse | A place
exam: «Shetland ponies from cold Scottish islands grow thick winter coats, so they are hardy.» Why are they called hardy? | Because they never need to eat | Because they live in hot places | *Because they can survive cold winters | Because they are small
